1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,244
Meeting rooms and shared equipment are booked the same way as meetings.

2
00:00:05,244 --> 00:00:09,157
This video shows how to add a Room and an Equipment calendar, how

3
00:00:09,157 --> 00:00:12,904
to book them by inviting them to an event, what happens when a

4
00:00:12,904 --> 00:00:16,707
room is already taken, and how to book or close a room straight

5
00:00:16,707 --> 00:00:18,140
on its own calendar.

6
00:00:22,746 --> 00:00:26,409
Room and Equipment calendars come with Resource Calendars.

7
00:00:26,409 --> 00:00:30,072
Open Manage Calendars, choose Add calendar, and then Room.

8
00:00:30,072 --> 00:00:33,792
Give it a Name, and fill in its Location, how many Seats it

9
00:00:33,792 --> 00:00:36,081
has, and what it is Equipped with.

10
00:00:36,081 --> 00:00:42,206
Rooms and equipment both come with the Resource Calendars feature, which your administrator turns on.

11
00:00:42,657 --> 00:00:47,658
A room starts as a Public calendar, so everyone sees when it is booked.

12
00:00:47,658 --> 00:00:52,269
Limit overlapping events starts ticked, with one event at a time.

13
00:00:52,269 --> 00:00:57,075
That limit is what makes a second booking for the same time refused.

14
00:00:57,075 --> 00:00:58,244
Choose Save.

15
00:00:58,244 --> 00:01:01,166
To retire a room later, untick Enabled:

16
00:01:01,166 --> 00:01:05,647
a disabled calendar keeps its events but takes no new bookings.

17
00:01:06,098 --> 00:01:09,362
An Equipment calendar is the same without seats.

18
00:01:09,362 --> 00:01:13,836
Here it is a demo projector, which also takes one booking at a time.

19
00:01:13,836 --> 00:01:16,799
Equipment is booked the same way as a room:

20
00:01:16,799 --> 00:01:21,031
it appears in the same Rooms and equipment list of an event, and

21
00:01:21,031 --> 00:01:24,598
one event can book a room and its projector together.

22
00:01:28,797 --> 00:01:31,626
To book a room, add an event as usual.

23
00:01:31,626 --> 00:01:37,089
Under Attendees, open Rooms and equipment, pick the Boardroom, and choose Save.

24
00:01:37,089 --> 00:01:40,367
The room is booked for the time of the event.

25
00:01:46,247 --> 00:01:48,510
The room has a calendar of its own.

26
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:52,430
Tick the Boardroom in the list on the side, and its bookings show

27
00:01:52,430 --> 00:01:54,307
for everyone who can see it.

28
00:01:54,307 --> 00:01:58,503
A booking that the room has declined does not count against its limit.

29
00:01:58,503 --> 00:02:02,257
Anyone who can see the room can look here to find a free time.

30
00:02:02,707 --> 00:02:06,143
Now another event at the same time in the same room.

31
00:02:06,143 --> 00:02:10,231
When it is saved, it is refused, and the editor stays open with

32
00:02:10,231 --> 00:02:13,490
a message saying that the room is already booked.

33
00:02:13,490 --> 00:02:17,459
The message names the room and the time that is taken, so you

34
00:02:17,459 --> 00:02:18,999
know what to change.

35
00:02:18,999 --> 00:02:22,791
Equipment, such as the projector, is refused the same way.

36
00:02:22,791 --> 00:02:26,227
Choose another time or another room, and save again.

37
00:02:30,429 --> 00:02:34,189
People who can change a room's calendar can add to it directly.

38
00:02:34,189 --> 00:02:37,459
New event lists the room with its two kinds of events:

39
00:02:37,459 --> 00:02:41,273
Booking, for a use of the room, and Maintenance, for the time it

40
00:02:41,273 --> 00:02:42,363
is out of use.

41
00:02:42,363 --> 00:02:46,614
The same limit applies, so maintenance blocks bookings of that time too.

42
00:02:46,614 --> 00:02:51,301
Because bookings and maintenance live on the room's calendar, anyone who can see

43
00:02:51,301 --> 00:02:54,789
the room can check when it is free before choosing a time.

44
00:02:56,789 --> 00:03:00,739
Add a calendar for each room and item, invite them to events to

45
00:03:00,739 --> 00:03:05,090
book them, and let the limit of one at a time keep the bookings apart.

46
00:03:05,090 --> 00:03:06,579
Thanks for watching.

